  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "DragHandleDirective implements low-level drag-and-drop functionality by listening to mouse events on a host element. It translates raw DOM events into structured DragEventData, applying movement restrictions based on the configured dragMode ('horizontal', 'vertical', or 'both'). Architecturally, it acts as a bridge, emitting events that allow parent components to manage the state of a larger draggable element, while managing global document listeners for precise tracking."
  },
